  "id": "BIT-rclone-2026-116192",
  "summary": "rclone from 1.37 before 1.74.2 SSRF via --rc-serve scheme-relative remote roots",
  "details": "rclone from 1.37 before 1.74.2 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to redirect http and netstorage backend requests by supplying a double-slash root on an existing named remote via --rc-serve. Attackers can make HEAD/GET requests to attacker-chosen hosts to read responses, capture configured custom headers, or obtain valid NetStorage request signatures.",
